<title>FINLAND: RAUMA'S TIMBERJACK WINS FIM 80 MLN ORDER.</title>
<headline>RAUMA'S TIMBERJACK WINS FIM 80 MLN ORDER.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1997-01-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Finnish engineering group Rauma Oy said on Thursday its Timberjack unit had sealed a deal to deliver forest machines worth 80 million markka to Russia and South America.  </p>
<p>Rauma said it had made contracts at the end of 1996 for delivery of 32 forest machines to South America and 43 forest machines to Russia.</p>
<p>&quot;Timberjack's susididiary in Sao Paulo, Brazil booked orders from Brazil, Chile and Uruguay during the last six weeks of the year,&quot; Rauma said in the statement.</p>
<p>The 80 million markka contracts now made public included 43 forest machines already delivered to Russia, Timberjack President and CEO Mikko Rysa said by telephone.</p>
<p>--John Acher, Helsinki Newsroom +358-9-680 50 235</p>
